    "recommendations": "• Install a reflective address marker at the street entrance to the driveway so responders can identify the property quickly from the road.\n• Mark the driveway entrance with reflective posts on both sides to define the entry point during low-light or smoky conditions.\n• Trim vegetation along both sides of the access drive to maintain a clear travel path wide enough for emergency vehicles.\n• Cut back any tree branches overhanging the access drive to allow ladder trucks and tall emergency vehicles to pass without obstruction.\n• Keep the access drive surface clear of debris, parked vehicles, and equipment that could block or slow an approaching emergency vehicle.\n• Identify and mark a turnaround area near the residence so emergency vehicles are not required to back out the full length of the driveway.\n• Clear a staging area near the residence where responders can position equipment and personnel without blocking the access drive.\n• Thin dense vegetation immediately alongside the access drive to reduce the risk of fire spreading across the driveway and cutting off the single access point.\n• Create a gap in dense vegetation between the open terrain and the residence so fire moving across open ground does not reach the structure unimpeded.\n• Post the property address visibly at the residence itself, not only at the street, so responders who have entered the property can confirm their location."
  },
