    "recommendations": "• Trim shrubs that are growing directly against the house walls and foundation.\n• Thin scattered trees near the structure to create open gaps between their canopies and the roofline.\n• Mow or cut down dry grass in the open areas immediately surrounding the structure.\n• Remove shrubs and tall grass growing along the edges of the single access driveway to keep it passable.\n• Keep overhanging tree branches trimmed back from above the roof and gutters.\n• Thin or remove shrubs clustered near any outbuildings or detached structures on the property.\n• Cut grass short in the open terrain areas closest to the house, particularly on the uphill or upwind sides.\n• Separate shrub groupings near the house so there are clear open gaps between each cluster.\n• Keep the full width of the driveway clear of encroaching vegetation to allow emergency vehicle access.\n• Remove dead grass, dead shrubs, and other dry plant material from around the base of the structure."
